[rvn-ple] Free loader-format MoE storage during the marlin repack

Only the RVN path reaches prepare_moe_nvfp4_layer_for_marlin: 0048 pins
--moe-runner-backend=marlin for the W4A16_NVFP4 checkpoint, while LIL runs the
same checkpoint family under flashinfer_cutlass and never enters this function.
Measured on a synthetic multi-layer NVFP4 MoE with the backend held fixed
(tests/rvn_ple/test_rvn_ple_moe_release.py), this branch peaked 0.0994 GiB above
the pre-layer baseline per layer where the fixed branch peaks 0.0427 GiB, and it
kept w13_blockscale_swizzled / w2_blockscale_swizzled -- loader-format scale
copies that create_weights allocated and that the marlin apply path only ever
reads through w*_weight_scale -- live for the process lifetime: 2 x scale bytes
per layer, ~7 GiB across the 48-layer RVN model, none of it reachable at
forward time.

Three fixes, all lifetime-only, with byte-identical repacked output (same
per-expert kernel results, same contiguous stack layout): release the dead
swizzle placeholders before repacking so their bytes fund the repack transients
instead of competing with them (the trtllm branch already drops them by
aliasing, and deepseek_v2's only other reader guards on hasattr); fill a
preallocated stack buffer expert-by-expert instead of holding a full per-expert
list plus its torch.stack copy; and drop each loader-format original as soon as
its repacked replacement is bound, so the whole layer no longer stays live
while the remaining repacks run. LIL is byte-identical: 0048's pin is the only
route to this function, and it is gated on is_w4a16_nvfp4.

